<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>African Parks: When conservation becomes a question of power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1466ba7c0c529905cbd51ba01c3d5315e695a552551cdf20d07647cc4e1041a</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372--4689a2636f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African Parks is dedicated to protecting wildlife on the continent across some vast areas. But the organization faces allegations of human rights abuses by rangers. Now, Prince Harry is stepping down from its board.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda: Traditional kingdom plunged into succession crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df736aa5df91eaef387982070d9a0a1e1a58ed182b52269dd6398785aff2e752</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-traditional-kingdom-plunged-into-succession-crisis/a-79214786--f0980c6e478f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-traditional-kingdom-plunged-into-succession-crisis/a-79214786?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A royal succession committee and the family of late King Oyo Nyimba of Toroo have put forward competing candidates. Questions have been raised as to whether the late monarch indeed had a son as his family claims.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta: Documents show Spanish intelligence warned of crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:106b0e05789a13bd53351fcef57051baed53def25b2223d714600f1b15066bd5</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505--1dd65a7f978d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain declassified documents that showed warnings issued a day before more than 70,000 migrants rushed the Ceuta border fence. Meanwhile, the EU announced funds to strengthen the border and return migrants to Morocco.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e172fe70f7153edb4ee378e1b9e62a24a57d1a1bb4aca7ae907f2d3220167dc4</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372e9691737e68a41488661b7518a4711aa0effb9f32de54573a802040f607c0</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco earthquake 3 years on: 'No one has remembered us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:798b99283bf1d0ad64de99a80dd603d18b75456994127e5ddebb7d594a8a9877</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844--cbd4f3eb032b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Morocco has rebuilt thousands of homes since the 2023 earthquake. But some survivors are still living in tents and say they have received no state aid.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
